{"term":"jealous","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:41465f4d4be57321ca","definition":"Suspecting rivalry in love; troubled by worries that one might have been replaced in someone's affections; suspicious of a lover's or spouse's fidelity.","example":"jealous lover","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous as a Barbary pigeon","jealous husbands problem","jealous-like","jealously","jealousness","jealousy","nonjealous","overjealous","superjealous","unjealous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b119f32ddf3a673507","definition":"Protective; zealously guarding; careful in the protection of something (or someone) one has or appreciates, especially one's spouse or lover.","example":"Thou ſhalt not bow downe thy ſelfe to them, nor ſerue them: For I the Lord thy God am a iealous God, viſiting the iniquitie of the fathers vpon the children, vnto the thirde and fourth generation of them that hate me:","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous as a Barbary pigeon","jealous husbands problem","jealous-like","jealously","jealousness","jealousy","nonjealous","overjealous","superjealous","unjealous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7735ab61ea67fd3d90","definition":"Envious; feeling resentful or angered toward someone for a perceived advantage or success, material or otherwise.","example":"be jealous of someone/something","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous as a Barbary pigeon","jealous husbands problem","jealous-like","jealously","jealousness","jealousy","nonjealous","overjealous","superjealous","unjealous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1facaf27aa54a00cdc","definition":"Suspicious; apprehensive.","example":"I began my fence or wall; which, being still jealous of my being attacked by somebody, I resolved to make very thick and strong.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous as a Barbary pigeon","jealous husbands problem","jealous-like","jealously","jealousness","jealousy","nonjealous","overjealous","superjealous","unjealous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fbc029740a5d1e25de","definition":"To harass or attack (somebody) out of jealousy.","example":"If I go back, he starts his jealousing again. Drinking and jealousing.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, slang","register":"ambitransitive, slang","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous as a Barbary pigeon","jealous husbands problem","jealous-like","jealously","jealousness","jealousy","nonjealous","overjealous","superjealous","unjealous"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jealous#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8764327508e3dce7c0","definition":"To deliberately make (someone) jealous of another person's (often their partner's) associations with other people.","example":"[…] where the victim of an assault had been 'jealousing' the offender about her sister.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["hyperjealous","jealous a